/-
  TinyVDB - Lean 4 formalization of the OpenVDB (`.vdb`) file format
  and the volume operators.

  The shipped marching-cubes lookup tables (`src/tinyvdb_mc_tri_table.h`,
  Bourke/Bloyd-derived canonical table, and `MC_EDGE_TABLE` in
  `src/tinyvdb_mesh.c`), with the table-level properties machine-checked:

  * `mcEdgeTable_eq_signChange` — **T-MC-EDGE** (both directions): for
    every case index k, bit e of `MC_EDGE_TABLE[k]` is set iff edge `e`
    is a sign-change edge of case `k` (0 mismatches; the C table was
    hand-verified at import time, now proof-checked);
  * `triIds_valid` / `trisTerminated` / `triCount_le_five` —
    **T-MC-COUNT**: every non 12 edge id is a valid edge (0..11), the
    triangle list terminates at the first 12 with only 12s after it, and
    every case has at most 5 triangles (15 integers);
  * `everySignChangeEdgeUsed` / `everyUsedEdgeSignChange` —
    **T-MC-COMPLETE**: every sign-change edge of a case appears in its
    emitted triangles (no dangling crossing), and every edge the table
    emits is a sign-change edge (the table never invents a crossing);
  * **`faceConsistent`** — **T-MC-FACE-CONSISTENT** (finding F10, upgraded
    from the `check_mc_face.py` script to a Lean theorem): on every
    ambiguous (checkerboard) face instance in all 256 cases (192 instances,
    12 face-bit patterns), the table pairs the four boundary crossing
    points by the *inside-corner* rule, uniformly — so two cubes sharing
    an ambiguous face always agree (no diagonal crack). The pairing depends
    only on the face's four sign bits;
  * **`boundarySegments_on_faces`** — **T-MC-BOUNDARY**: on every face of
    the cube, the mod-2 boundary edges of the emitted triangles lie on
    that face and pair exactly its sign-change edges (all 256 cases).

  All proofs are `native_decide` over the 256 cases. The tables are
  embedded verbatim from the shipped headers.

